00:00:10.266 --> 00:00:12.533
Let's answer that question in more detail today

00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:16.166
Board painting is essentially painting with electronic devices

00:00:16.300 --> 00:00:19.533
There are four core differences from hand drawing

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:22.266
The first difference is that it can be withdrawn

00:00:22.700 --> 00:00:24.666
If you're not happy with the result of your stroke

00:00:24.666 --> 00:00:26.599
You can go all the way back to the previous step

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:28.533
Time can be turned back

00:00:28.766 --> 00:00:30.299
And this is in traditional hand painting tools

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:31.966
A state that is impossible to achieve

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.066
This feature leads to huge operations

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.199
Ease of modification

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.600
The second core difference is the layer function

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.866
Layers are a unique feature of board painting

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.166
Layers in a nutshell

00:00:42.166 --> 00:00:43.499
Is to take the final result

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.666
Step by step, layer by layer

00:00:45.966 --> 00:00:47.499
The concept was articulated

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.866
Is in modern cartography

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:50.666
According to this idea

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.100
Computer CD drawing line and color

00:00:53.100 --> 00:00:54.600
Not all at once

00:00:54.600 --> 00:00:56.000
It's layering

00:00:56.100 --> 00:00:58.100
I just draw one part of it every time

00:00:58.333 --> 00:01:00.066
There are professional commercial illustrators

00:01:00.066 --> 00:01:02.999
A drawing may be drawn in hundreds of layers

00:01:03.533 --> 00:01:05.866
So let's look at the process of painting an airplane

00:01:05.866 --> 00:01:08.566
